        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(session-memory): bound session transcript reads to prevent OOM",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`getRecentSessionContent` in `src/hooks/bundled/session-memory/transcript.ts` reads session transcript JSONL files with an unbounded `fs.promises.readFile` call. A runaway or corrupted session file could force the session-memory extraction path to buffer the entire file into memory, leading to OOM.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nSession-memory extraction now streams the transcript newest-first through the shared `streamSessionTranscriptLinesReverse` helper, collects up to the 16 MiB tail, and reverses the collected tail lines back into chronological order before running the existing sanitizer/provenance filter pipeline. The byte cap is enforced before each line is retained, so an oversized early record is excluded rather than buffered.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSession-memory extraction now safely bounds oversized transcripts while still keeping the most recent messages available for context.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Added a regression test that writes a transcript exceeding the 16 MiB cap with recent trailing messages and asserts:\n  - the recent messages are preserved,\n  - the huge early message is absent,\n  - the returned memory content stays under the 16 MiB cap.\n- Local focused run: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/hooks/bundled/session-memory/transcript.test.ts --run` passes (4/4 tests).\n\n## Real behavior proof (standalone)\n\nI ran a standalone Node script outside Vitest that imports the actual changed helper from source (`src/hooks/bundled/session-memory/transcript.ts`) and exercises a transcript larger than the 16 MiB cap where the trailing lines contain recent messages.\n\nScript: `/tmp/proof-101475.mjs` (not committed).\n\n```text\n$ node --import tsx /tmp/proof-101475.mjs\n=== Oversized transcript ===\nFile size: 17826089 bytes (cap is 16777216 bytes)\nResult contains recent user message: true\nResult contains recent assistant message: true\nResult does NOT contain the huge early message: true\nResult length under cap: true\n```\n\nThe helper streams only the tail of the oversized file through the shared reverse reader, stops before retaining the over-cap early record, and returns the recent messages without buffering the entire transcript into memory.\n",
